          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of the Wright Brothers</strong><br>\nWilbur and Orville Wright, known as the Wright brothers, were American inventors and pioneers of aviation. Born in Indiana and Ohio respectively, they developed an interest in flying from a young age. Their curiosity was sparked by a toy helicopter their father gave them, leading to a lifelong fascination with flight.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Wright Brothers' Education</strong><br>\nDespite neither brother receiving a formal college education, they were intellectually curious and self-taught in many areas. They used their self-acquired skills to open a printing press and later, a bicycle repair shop and factory. Their mechanical expertise gained from bicycles played a crucial role in their aviation experiments.</p>\n\n<p><strong>First Steps Toward Flight</strong><br>\nThe Wright brothers' journey towards flight began with extensive research and study of earlier attempts at aviation. They read about and observed birds in flight to understand how wings worked. This observation led them to test their theories through several experiments including the creation of kites and gliders.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
